==Question #6==
{{Cquote2|Weapon doesn’t have any strict drawbacks like scythe/tbow, is it too strong?}}

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tfyfk9a4GJ0&t=622s Youtube Time Stamp]

* '''Mod Arcane:''' Scythe can only be used realistically on a 3x3, Tbow can only be used effectively on monsters with 200+ Magic level. That is seen as a restriction, but in reality, it's not really much of a restriction. Most bosses in the game are 3x3 or above and the Scythe is pretty good at that. Tbows good at a lot of monsters so it's not really niche, it's a fake niche. But I get the point, it gives you a different way to balance a weapon and give other weapons viability.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' What we're leaning on here is the fact that you need quite a lot of magic switches for this weapon to get really, really powerful and worth using. That's the drawback - if you only want to bring Sang or a one way switch, this weapon isn't very good, and obviously you're going to lose all the healing from Sang, if you're comparing it to that. If we do eventually get around to rebalancing Elemental, Harm, etc. Harm would still have its purpose, its power.
* '''Mod Arcane:''' So we don't think it's necessary, but again, give us feedback if you feel like it's too strong! It's obviously an iterative process.

==Question #7==
{{Cquote2|Can Harmonised staff be buffed? Can you fix the autocast on it?}}

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tfyfk9a4GJ0&t=687s Youtube Time Stamp]

